        "original_id": "5db7a355-75bb-5a62-a70f-0e65af7f904f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Sidney Herbert Sime, Lord Dunsany, Queen Victoria\n- Roles: artist, author, monarch\n- Places: England, Ireland, United Kingdom\n- Topics: Victorian era, fantastic art, satirical art, story illustration\n\nFacts:\n- Queen Victoria reigned over the United Kingdom from 20 June 1837 until her death on 22 January 1901, and this period is known as the Victorian era.\n- Sidney Herbert Sime was an English artist who lived from 1865 to 22 May 1941 and was often called S. H. Sime.\n- Sidney Herbert Sime worked in the late Victorian and succeeding periods.\n- Sidney Herbert Sime is mostly remembered for fantastic and satirical artwork.\n- Sidney Herbert Sime especially illustrated stories by the Irish author Lord Dunsany.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
